{"cells":[{"kind":1,"language":"markdown","value":"# Units\n\nThis module demonstrates the use of Units of Measure (UoM) in **e-lang**.\n\nIn e-lang, the UoM are a first class citizen of the language. Behind the scenes, a `measurement` type is a combination of a `number` and a `unit` type.\n\nThe `unit` type belongs to a `unit_family`.\n\nLet's start by defining a `unit_family` called **Length** with two units in it: **milimitres** and **inches**.\n\nInside the `unit_family` definition, we also include the appropriate conversion formulas between them."},{"kind":2,"language":"e-lang","value":"domain Units\n\nunit_family Length \"This family contains units that represent the physical length of objects\" {\n    unit mm:milimetre \"Length in the international system\"\n    unit m:metre \n    unit in:inch \"Length in the imperial system\"\n\n    conversion m->mm: (val: number_[Length]) => val * 1000\n    conversion mm->in: (val) => val / 2.54\n    conversion in->mm: (val) => val * 2.54\n}\n\nprint 1000_[mm]->in\nprint 100_[m]^2\n\n// Declare a variable to represent a length measurement of 10 mm\nconst len_m = 1_[m]\nprint \"Original lenght as defined in metres: \" + len_m\n\n// Convert this measurement to 'mm'\nprint \"Conversion of metres to milimetres: \" + len_m->mm\n\n// Convert this measurement to 'in'\nprint \"Conversion of milimetres to inches: \" + len_m->mm->in\n\n// Declare a variable to represent a length measurement of 5 in\nconst len_in = 5_[in]\nprint \"Define a new length in inches: \" + len_in\n\n// Convert this measurement to 'mm'\nprint \"Conversion of inches to milimetres: \" + len_in->mm\n\n// Units can also be used in operations\nconst sum_of_len = len_m->mm + len_in\n// The calculated value of different units in the same family\n// defaults to the unit of the last expression in the operation\nprint \"Sum of lengths in milimetres and inches: \" + sum_of_len\n\n// The result of operations can also be converted to a desired unit\nprint \"Sum result converted to milimetres: \" + sum_of_len->mm\n"},{"kind":1,"language":"markdown","value":"## Unit Operations"},{"kind":2,"language":"e-lang","value":"domain UnitOperations\n\nunit_family Length \"This family contains units that represent the physical length of objects\" {\n    unit mm:milimetre \"Length in the international system\"\n    unit m:metre \n    unit in:inch \"Length in the imperial system\"\n\n    conversion m->mm: (val: number_[Length]) => val * 1000\n    conversion mm->m: (val) => val / 1000\n    conversion mm->in: (val: number_[Length]) => val / 2.54\n    conversion in->mm: (val: number_[Length]) => val * 2.54\n}\n\nunit_family Area {\n    unit m2:square_metre\n    unit ft2:square_foot\n\n    conversion m2->ft2: (val: number_[Area]) => val * 10.7639\n    conversion ft2->m2: (val: number_[Area]) => val / 10.7639\n    conversion m->m2: (val1: number_[Length], val2: number_[Length]) => val1 * val2\n}\n\nconst length1 = 10_[m]\nconst length2 = 500_[mm]\n\nconst area1 = length2 * length1\n\nprint area1\n\n// print 10_[m]->m2(10_[m])\n\n// Causes type error\n// print 10_[m] + 10_[m2]"},{"kind":2,"language":"e-lang","value":"unit_family Length {\n  unit m:meter\n  unit yd:yard\n\n  conversion m->yd: (val: number_[Length]) => val * 1.09361\n  conversion yd->m: (val: number_[Length]) => val / 1.09361\n}\n\nunit_family Temperature {\n  unit degC:DegreesCentigrade\n  unit degF:DegreesFahrenheit\n}\n\nunit_family Mass {\n  unit kg:kilogram\n  unit lb:pound\n}\n\nunit_family Other {\n  unit item:item\n}\n\nunit_family Time {\n  unit sec:second\n  unit m:minute\n}\n\n// 4\nconst length = 10_[m]\n\n// 5\nconst mass = 5_[kg]\n\n// 6\nconst time = 2_[sec]\n\n// 7\nconst measurementTimesNumber = length * 2\n\n// 8\nconst numberTimesMeasurement = 3 * length\n\n// 9\nconst measurementTimesMeasurement = length * time\n\n// 10\nconst measurementDividedByNumber = length / 2\n\n// 11\nconst numberDividedByMeasurement = 2 / length\n\n// 12\nconst measurementDividedByMeasurement = length / mass\n\nprint time\nprint length\nprint mass\nprint measurementTimesNumber\nprint numberTimesMeasurement\nprint measurementTimesMeasurement\nprint measurementDividedByNumber\nprint numberDividedByMeasurement\nprint measurementDividedByMeasurement"}]}